# Base map tile archive.
#
# Left unset, the app reads /tiles/basemap.pmtiles from its own origin: in
# production that is the Cloudflare Worker serving the archive out of R2, and
# in development it is the local file at ./tiles/basemap.pmtiles, which
# `npm run tiles` downloads. See "Base map" in README.md.
#
# Set this to point a local dev server at a deployed instance or at a public
# R2 bucket URL instead of keeping a copy of the archive on disk, e.g.
#   VITE_PMTILES_URL=https://navsar.example.org/tiles/basemap.pmtiles
# The URL must allow cross-origin range requests, or the map will not draw and
# the PDF export will lose its base layer to canvas tainting.
VITE_PMTILES_URL=
